      "body": "Thanks for this :)\r\n\r\nSo bringing back my comment https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35436#issuecomment-4924788369\r\n\r\nMaybe not adding all of them as I initially suggested, but for example #34861 needs, apart from the ones this PR adds:\r\n```c++\r\nenum class WalletErrorCode {\r\n        INVALID_DESCRIPTOR,\r\n        INVALID_PARAMETER,\r\n        MISC_ERROR\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nAre we open to add those to this enum, even if some like `INVALID_DESCRIPTOR` are not as much generic as others?\r\nIf we don't then we need multiple structs to handle different error codes which adds a lot of complexity.",
